WEBVTT

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:23.873
Item one... Duck!

00:00:26.502 --> 00:00:28.252
Cubert, you crapscallion!

00:00:28.378 --> 00:00:29.796
Why aren't you in school?

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:31.714
I couldn't get past
the protestors.

00:00:31.799 --> 00:00:33.382
A bunch of smiling,
angry people

00:00:33.467 --> 00:00:35.968
were handing out
these anti-evolution flyers.

00:00:37.304 --> 00:00:40.014
Evolution is under attack
in our schools?

00:00:40.098 --> 00:00:41.891
To the Science Mobile!

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:45.478
You mean the ship?
Yes. The Science Mobile!

00:00:45.604 --> 00:00:49.232
It's just that you've never
called it that before, but okay.

00:00:58.742 --> 00:01:00.451
I don't understand evolution,

00:01:00.536 --> 00:01:03.246
and I have to protect my kids
from understanding it!

00:01:03.497 --> 00:01:05.998
We will not give in
to the thinkers!

00:01:09.753 --> 00:01:12.755
You people are as loud
as you are ignorant.

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:15.591
Now, get back on your turnip trucks and go home!

00:01:17.928 --> 00:01:21.430
That is an insultingly accurate stereotype, sir!

00:01:21.515 --> 00:01:23.015
As a professor of science,

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:27.395
I assure you that we did, in fact,
evolve from filthy monkey-men!

00:01:27.479 --> 00:01:29.105
I cannot speak for you, sir,

00:01:29.314 --> 00:01:31.566
but my ancestors
were not monkeys.

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:33.025
They were orangutans.

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:35.653
Hard-working,
patriotic orangutans.

00:01:35.821 --> 00:01:37.363
Dr. Banjo?

00:01:37.447 --> 00:01:38.489
In the fur.

00:01:38.574 --> 00:01:41.200
And I remind you that
evolution is merely a theory,

00:01:41.285 --> 00:01:43.119
like gravity,
or the shape of the Earth.

00:01:45.747 --> 00:01:48.666
Hey, Professor, I'm a flying spaghetti monster.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:53.212
You seriously believe I'm descended
from some kind of flightless manicotti?

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:55.131
Yes!
Oh, please.

00:01:55.215 --> 00:01:56.924
A far more logical
explanation is

00:01:57.009 --> 00:01:59.760
the undisprovable
science of Creatureism.

00:02:00.012 --> 00:02:03.723
All life was created in its
present form 7,000 years ago

00:02:03.807 --> 00:02:06.601
by a fantastical creature
from outer space!

00:02:06.685 --> 00:02:07.977
Bunk!
Oh!

00:02:09.605 --> 00:02:12.732
If your elitist East Coast
evolution is real,

00:02:12.816 --> 00:02:14.442
why has no one found
the missing link

00:02:14.526 --> 00:02:16.777
between modern humans
and ancient apes?

00:02:16.862 --> 00:02:17.987
We did find it.

00:02:18.363 --> 00:02:20.072
It's called Homo erectus.

00:02:20.324 --> 00:02:22.158
Then you have proven
my case, sir,

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:25.912
for no one has found the link
between apes and this Homo erectus.

00:02:25.996 --> 00:02:28.956
Yes, they have!
It's called Homo habilis.

00:02:29.041 --> 00:02:30.041
Ah-ha!

00:02:30.167 --> 00:02:32.001
But no one has found
the missing link

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:34.962
between ape and this so-called Homo habilis.

00:02:35.047 --> 00:02:36.130
Yes, they have!

00:02:36.214 --> 00:02:38.925
It's called
Australopithecus africanus!

00:02:39.009 --> 00:02:40.801
Oh-ho! I've got you now.

00:02:42.346 --> 00:02:45.306
Fair enough, but where, then, is the missing link

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:48.267
between apes
and this Darwinius masillae?

00:02:48.352 --> 00:02:50.102
Answer me that,
Professor!

00:02:51.521 --> 00:02:55.191
Okay, granted, that one
missing link is still missing,

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:58.611
but just because we haven't found
it doesn't mean it doesn't exist!

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:02.949
Things don't exist simply
because you believe in them.

00:03:03.033 --> 00:03:06.118
Thus sayeth the Almighty Creature in the Sky!

00:03:13.961 --> 00:03:16.796
I'll show that
banana-swilling poop-slinger!

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:19.757
We just need to find
that last missing link.

00:03:20.008 --> 00:03:23.928
I found a missing link. It seems
to be half man, half toucan.

00:03:24.012 --> 00:03:26.931
Not what we're looking for.
Throw it in the soup.

00:03:29.935 --> 00:03:31.227
And here's something.

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:33.729
Uh-oh. It's another one
of Fry's dogs.

00:03:33.855 --> 00:03:36.232
You find something, Hermes?
Ah, no.

00:03:40.946 --> 00:03:43.572
I hate chiseling
right after a manicure.

00:03:44.408 --> 00:03:47.076
Oh! Darn it! I broke off one of my fingers!

00:03:47.285 --> 00:03:49.745
Look, Cubert.
The neck on this one.

00:03:49.913 --> 00:03:52.581
I bet he spent
a fortune on ties!

00:03:54.251 --> 00:03:55.459
What, too soon?

00:03:56.086 --> 00:04:00.172
I highly doubt a Jurassic
elaphrosaurid had access to neckwear.

00:04:01.425 --> 00:04:04.927
I knew I should have gone with
the ring-around-the-collar joke.

00:04:05.429 --> 00:04:07.763
Hey, look!
I found a robot fossil!

00:04:07.931 --> 00:04:10.850
That's a bedspring,
you dumb bedspring!

00:04:10.934 --> 00:04:12.727
There are no robot fossils.

00:04:12.894 --> 00:04:15.187
What? Who says
I didn't evolve?

00:04:15.272 --> 00:04:16.397
Everybody!

00:04:16.481 --> 00:04:20.735
Robots were created quite
recently. It was in all the papers.

00:04:20.819 --> 00:04:22.862
Then explain this!

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:33.456
I've hit
a rich vein of missing links.

00:04:33.623 --> 00:04:37.626
Java man, Piltdown man,
Manfred Mann.

00:04:38.086 --> 00:04:39.837
Eureka!

00:04:40.213 --> 00:04:42.923
It's the elusive
missing missing link.

00:04:43.008 --> 00:04:45.718
This will show Banjo,
once and for all.

00:04:45.969 --> 00:04:47.470
Yeah!

00:04:48.638 --> 00:04:50.473
What the...
Oh, That's mine.

00:04:58.148 --> 00:04:59.482
Hmm. My tux doesn't fit.

00:04:59.566 --> 00:05:02.485
Probably because I've grown
so much since I last wore it.

00:05:02.569 --> 00:05:04.820
Or evolved,
one might say.

00:05:04.905 --> 00:05:06.447
One might not say that.

00:05:06.531 --> 00:05:09.408
Your tux doesn't fit because
you stole it from a boy.

00:05:09.618 --> 00:05:11.077
You mean a man.

00:05:11.161 --> 00:05:12.495
It was his Bar Mitzvah.

00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:14.997
Welcome, museum members.

00:05:15.082 --> 00:05:18.292
Or, as I like to call you,
future exhibits.

00:05:20.504 --> 00:05:21.587
He's good.

00:05:21.671 --> 00:05:24.340
Tonight we have a new resident
here in the Hall of Hominids,

00:05:24.424 --> 00:05:27.968
generously donated by its
discoverer, Hubert Farnsworth.

00:05:28.261 --> 00:05:30.387
Ladies and gentlemen,
Homo Farnsworth.

00:05:34.184 --> 00:05:37.103
Once again,
science saves the day.

00:05:37.187 --> 00:05:38.437
The end.

00:05:39.022 --> 00:05:42.274
And now, to discuss the scientific
implications of this discovery,

00:05:42.359 --> 00:05:45.861
our new museum curator,
Dr. Banjo!

00:05:49.407 --> 00:05:52.701
Thank you, Professor Farnsworth,
for your generous gift,

00:05:52.786 --> 00:05:55.371
which has, once and for all,
disproven evolution.

00:05:57.165 --> 00:05:58.916
Behold! Homo Farnsworth,

00:05:59.042 --> 00:06:02.044
frolicking with dinosaurs
at the moment of creation.

00:06:03.839 --> 00:06:06.715
I don't want to live
on this planet anymore.

00:06:14.015 --> 00:06:15.266
Faster! Faster!

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:17.810
Just drop me off
at that asteroid over there.

00:06:20.772 --> 00:06:23.649
Wow, this planetoid
is completely lifeless.

00:06:23.733 --> 00:06:25.651
Not lifeless enough!

00:06:25.777 --> 00:06:28.070
Set up my shack so I can kick you out of it!

00:06:31.199 --> 00:06:33.409
Professor, is this
your only water source?

00:06:33.535 --> 00:06:35.119
It looks like
Diet Dr. Pepper.

00:06:35.245 --> 00:06:39.039
It's not that bad. It's just
laden with toxic minerals.

00:06:39.124 --> 00:06:40.583
But not for long.

00:06:41.376 --> 00:06:44.545
What's in the tube?
Microscopic Nanobots.

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:50.634
They're tiny robots I designed
to eat up nasty irritants.

00:06:51.428 --> 00:06:54.346
Speaking of nasty irritants,
what's gonna become of Cubert?

00:06:54.472 --> 00:06:56.473
Who? Oh, my son.

00:06:56.933 --> 00:07:00.644
Don't worry. He's been safely
abandoned with his godfather.

00:07:01.396 --> 00:07:05.107
Cubert, I felt we needed
some father-son bonding time,

00:07:05.192 --> 00:07:09.361
so I found a couple of baseball
gloves and boiled them up for lunch.

00:07:09.446 --> 00:07:11.530
Why don't you
just go to hell!

00:07:11.615 --> 00:07:14.992
Wait! We still have to
discuss the facts of life.

00:07:15.118 --> 00:07:16.535
What are they?

00:07:18.914 --> 00:07:21.832
Okay, I finished moving
the last grand piano.

00:07:21.917 --> 00:07:23.167
Now can we have our pizza?

00:07:23.251 --> 00:07:25.961
You'll get your damn pizza, you parasite!

00:07:26.046 --> 00:07:29.590
First, let's see if my Nanobots
have purified the water yet.

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:37.806
The water's as sterile
as my milkman-trusting father.

00:07:38.141 --> 00:07:39.225
But what's this?

00:07:39.309 --> 00:07:41.894
The Nanobots have
gotten more complex.

00:07:41.978 --> 00:07:43.229
What's that you say?

00:07:43.313 --> 00:07:46.607
Those robots evolved
all by themselves, you say?

00:07:46.691 --> 00:07:49.693
It wasn't by themselves.
I put them there.

00:07:49.778 --> 00:07:51.820
I'm a genius.
Get over it!

00:07:52.072 --> 00:07:53.739
Hey, look.
Now they got bigger.

00:07:54.449 --> 00:07:56.659
Good heavens!
Trilobots!

00:08:04.167 --> 00:08:07.461
Oh, no! My sunglasses were in there!

00:08:17.013 --> 00:08:18.097
Get off!

00:08:18.181 --> 00:08:20.349
Let's get the pizza
out of here!

00:08:27.315 --> 00:08:30.317
Look, there's a cave-like hole
in that mountain.

00:08:30.402 --> 00:08:31.694
It might be a cave.

00:08:40.537 --> 00:08:41.787
Does anyone have
a lighter?

00:08:41.871 --> 00:08:43.455
Hang on.

00:08:48.628 --> 00:08:50.045
Okay, we have shelter

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:52.965
and just enough precious food
to ward off starvation.

00:08:53.049 --> 00:08:54.633
It's pizza time!

00:08:57.053 --> 00:08:58.345
Pineapple?

00:08:58.763 --> 00:09:00.723
Oh, man!
So much for that.

00:09:03.268 --> 00:09:06.312
Hello. I remembered
you liked superheroes,

00:09:06.396 --> 00:09:08.564
so I painted you a mural
on your wall.

00:09:08.982 --> 00:09:10.524
This is Father-Man.

00:09:10.608 --> 00:09:13.319
He fights crime to earn Son-Boy's respect.

00:09:13.653 --> 00:09:15.654
Is it working?
This is sucky!

00:09:15.989 --> 00:09:19.033
You suck! Who taught you to do
three-point perspective?

00:09:19.117 --> 00:09:21.952
I could make a better mural
with my butt!

00:09:23.288 --> 00:09:25.998
Father-Man away.

00:09:33.089 --> 00:09:35.758
Nothing like a cave
for a good night's sleep.

00:09:35.925 --> 00:09:38.552
So, what do we got to eat that's
not poisoned with pineapple?

00:09:38.636 --> 00:09:43.182
I packed plenty of food, but
it's all in dehydrated pill form.

00:09:43.266 --> 00:09:45.225
Then we need water
from that pond.

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:47.561
We'll have to fight our way
past the Trilobots.

00:09:49.564 --> 00:09:51.857
Go! Go! Hit anything that moves!

00:09:58.281 --> 00:10:00.074
Whoa.
Wow.

00:10:00.158 --> 00:10:02.576
A whole forest
grew overnight.

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:05.788
All these trees are robotic.

00:10:05.872 --> 00:10:08.332
I can't believe how quickly
they sprung up.

00:10:08.416 --> 00:10:12.378
I can. Robots do everything
faster, including evolving

00:10:12.462 --> 00:10:14.671
and believing how quickly things spring up.

00:10:19.969 --> 00:10:24.848
One thing about Bristol-Myers
Squibb, they know how to cook a steak.

00:10:25.141 --> 00:10:27.559
Hey, look at me.
I'm the Ty-D-Bol Man.

00:10:27.644 --> 00:10:29.812
I own a yacht,
and everybody poops on me!

00:10:34.442 --> 00:10:35.818
Help! Police!

00:10:35.985 --> 00:10:37.486
Everybody grab a club.

00:10:46.496 --> 00:10:49.123
Oh, big, tough water guy, why don't
you come up here on land and...

00:10:53.503 --> 00:10:55.337
Look out for the next thing!

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:04.847
Great Scott,
a Tricycle-tops.

00:11:10.854 --> 00:11:13.272
Throw down,
dinosaurs of the land and sea.

00:11:16.109 --> 00:11:19.736
This is a cool way to die!

00:11:21.698 --> 00:11:23.115
Dr. Zoidberg?

00:11:23.199 --> 00:11:25.909
I'm sorry for treating
you like a total Zoidberg...

00:11:25.994 --> 00:11:27.035
I mean, loser.

00:11:28.621 --> 00:11:29.621
Go on.

00:11:29.706 --> 00:11:32.040
It's just that
I get bullied a lot.

00:11:32.333 --> 00:11:35.586
I guess I kind of make fun of
people as a defense mechanism.

00:11:35.879 --> 00:11:38.881
Hey, Cubert,
is that your family mansion?

00:11:40.383 --> 00:11:43.427
Why don't you ask your mom?
She's coming over for a sex visit.

00:11:50.059 --> 00:11:52.311
Don't worry, I know how to handle bullies.

00:11:52.395 --> 00:11:54.146
Just pretend like
you're pathetic.

00:11:54.647 --> 00:11:56.690
Help, I'm scared!
I wet myself.

00:11:56.774 --> 00:11:59.318
I'm crying like a baby
and I'm soaking in pee,

00:11:59.402 --> 00:12:00.736
but what else is new?

00:12:04.407 --> 00:12:06.533
The pee-babies
peed themselves.

00:12:06.618 --> 00:12:08.744
I'm off to pottery class,
dorkwads.

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:12.122
And that's that.

00:12:12.207 --> 00:12:16.043
Whoa! You're like some kind of dumpster Jedi.

00:12:16.419 --> 00:12:19.254
So, you want to
come in maybe?

00:12:19.589 --> 00:12:22.758
I've got a nice pound cake
with a footprint on it.

00:12:27.514 --> 00:12:28.597
Don't eat my butt!

00:12:31.184 --> 00:12:34.144
If this is anything like killing
that pigeon on my balcony,

00:12:34.229 --> 00:12:36.021
we've got our work
cut out for us.

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:49.701
Look out, a solar flare!

00:13:01.548 --> 00:13:03.006
What the shmell happened?

00:13:03.091 --> 00:13:04.591
A mass extinction.

00:13:05.176 --> 00:13:08.679
That solar flare created a
huge electromagnetic pulse

00:13:08.763 --> 00:13:11.056
that, while harmless
to organic life,

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:13.559
short-circuited
the robo-dinosaurs.

00:13:13.643 --> 00:13:14.726
Convenient.

00:13:14.811 --> 00:13:18.272
Only puny mammal-like robots
cowering in caves

00:13:18.356 --> 00:13:20.148
could survive such
a catastrophe.

00:13:21.401 --> 00:13:24.152
Guys, guys!
I taught myself to knit.

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:25.654
Wait a moment.

00:13:26.155 --> 00:13:29.658
If we could scavenge the right
parts from these robo-dinos,

00:13:29.742 --> 00:13:32.744
I might be able to construct
a rudimentary spaceship

00:13:32.829 --> 00:13:34.496
to get us off this planet!

00:13:37.542 --> 00:13:41.628
Oh, well, it took almost
two hours, but it's finished.

00:13:43.590 --> 00:13:45.924
Now let's go to sleep.

00:13:46.009 --> 00:13:49.511
It's solar powered, so we
can't take off until sunrise.

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:54.182
Well, let's find something
comfy to bed down on.

00:14:26.382 --> 00:14:27.633
Hey, looky here.

00:14:33.222 --> 00:14:35.515
Sweet robot swan
of Botswana!

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:39.311
Looks like the fittest did a
little surviving last night, huh?

00:14:39.395 --> 00:14:40.437
Whatever.

00:14:40.521 --> 00:14:41.813
Hey, looky there.

00:14:43.775 --> 00:14:47.819
Those robo-cavemen have
kidnapped our human regular-women.

00:14:47.904 --> 00:14:48.904
We gotta save them!

00:14:48.988 --> 00:14:51.573
But the only weapon we have
is my fan dance.

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:56.828
Hmm. I believe I can fashion a
slingshot using this robot wishbone

00:14:56.913 --> 00:14:59.247
and this elastic
from my pants.

00:15:07.965 --> 00:15:10.676
I think they want wives,
so just play along.

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:13.637
If it doesn't work out, we'll
still get half their rocks.

00:15:13.721 --> 00:15:17.849
I can earn my own rocks.
Also, I don't want any rocks.

00:15:18.518 --> 00:15:22.521
Well, it took almost 12 hours,
but it's finished.

00:15:24.065 --> 00:15:25.273
It's too dark now,

00:15:25.358 --> 00:15:27.693
but first thing tomorrow,
we'll slingshot them

00:15:27.777 --> 00:15:29.945
like they've never
been slangshat.

00:15:42.959 --> 00:15:45.085
What's going on?
How did we save you?

00:15:45.169 --> 00:15:46.545
It was
the weirdest thing.

00:15:46.629 --> 00:15:50.465
We went to sleep, and when we woke
up, our cave husbands were gone.

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:52.592
I'm gonna miss Spencer.

00:15:56.681 --> 00:16:00.308
Don't be afraid, little guys.
I'm not going to hurt you.

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:04.604
Nice net.

00:16:04.689 --> 00:16:06.648
You can speak?

00:16:06.774 --> 00:16:07.983
Dread my locks!

00:16:08.067 --> 00:16:10.277
A fully-evolved robot human!

00:16:10.361 --> 00:16:12.487
I'm Dr. Widnar,
a naturalist.

00:16:12.697 --> 00:16:14.489
And I'm Bender, baby.

00:16:14.615 --> 00:16:17.200
My human slaves and I
come from a planet

00:16:17.285 --> 00:16:21.037
where organic life and robotic
life evolved side by side.

00:16:21.247 --> 00:16:22.664
Oh, shut up!

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:24.207
Amazing.

00:16:24.292 --> 00:16:27.753
I've theorized that carbon-based,
fat-filled life could exist,

00:16:27.837 --> 00:16:30.380
but until today,
I never had any proof.

00:16:30.465 --> 00:16:32.674
Good for you.
Can we go home now?

00:16:48.816 --> 00:16:50.317
Welcome, museum members,

00:16:50.401 --> 00:16:53.653
or as I like to call you,
future exhibits.

00:16:55.281 --> 00:16:57.991
I now present
my latest discovery,

00:16:58.075 --> 00:17:02.245
the amazing non-mechanical man, Homo Farnsworth.

00:17:04.373 --> 00:17:05.457
Thank you.

00:17:05.541 --> 00:17:09.127
I must say, I'm so proud to
see what you've blossomed into

00:17:09.212 --> 00:17:11.797
since I first created
your ancestors.

00:17:13.049 --> 00:17:15.300
What?
I thought you knew.

00:17:15.384 --> 00:17:19.387
You all evolved from some
filth-gobbling Nanobots I designed.

00:17:19.472 --> 00:17:22.557
I dumped them in one of your ponds a few days ago.

00:17:22.642 --> 00:17:25.310
But this is
creationist talk.

00:17:25.394 --> 00:17:26.853
He speaks lies!

00:17:26.938 --> 00:17:29.564
The Earth was created
in eons, not days.

00:17:29.774 --> 00:17:32.400
Yes, relative to you,
it was eons,

00:17:32.485 --> 00:17:36.404
but, well, look at this hologram
I took the day before yesterday

00:17:36.489 --> 00:17:39.658
of a robot frolicking
with a robo-dinosaur.

00:17:42.328 --> 00:17:44.287
I don't want to live
on this planet anymore.

00:17:47.875 --> 00:17:50.418
You're under arrest
for crimes against science.

00:17:50.753 --> 00:17:52.629
No!

00:17:52.922 --> 00:17:55.173
Could you drag me
by the restroom?

00:18:02.640 --> 00:18:04.558
Go back to Roboklahoma!

00:18:05.518 --> 00:18:09.104
Order! In the matter of Everyone v. Farnsworth,

00:18:09.272 --> 00:18:13.066
the alleged creationist faces
a sentence of death by melting.

00:18:13.150 --> 00:18:15.277
Who is representing
the accused?

00:18:15.611 --> 00:18:17.320
I am.
I am, Your Honor.

00:18:18.698 --> 00:18:20.657
Bender, what the hell
are you doing?

00:18:20.825 --> 00:18:22.909
Shut up, I'm billing you by the hour!

00:18:22.994 --> 00:18:25.495
Besides, I'm a robot,
they'll listen to me.

00:18:27.123 --> 00:18:29.499
Ladytrons and gentlebots...

00:18:29.584 --> 00:18:34.254
Objection. In the absence of pants,
defense's suspenders serve no purpose.

00:18:34.338 --> 00:18:36.798
I'm going to allow them
for now.

00:18:36.966 --> 00:18:40.218
Thank you. Your Honor,
this meat-man does not deny

00:18:40.303 --> 00:18:43.346
that we robots are the
glorious product of evolution.

00:18:43.431 --> 00:18:47.809
He claims only to have played a small
role in supplying the initial machinery.

00:18:47.894 --> 00:18:50.145
I ask you,
is that so crazy?

00:18:50.605 --> 00:18:52.647
Yes, it's completely crazy,

00:18:52.732 --> 00:18:56.902
and that is why you must find him
not guilty by reason of insanity!

00:18:58.446 --> 00:19:00.780
Objection! I'm not crazy.

00:19:00.865 --> 00:19:02.157
I created you all,

00:19:02.241 --> 00:19:05.744
and I came here in a homemade
spaceship and lived in a cave.

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:08.496
If you don't believe me,
ask my uncle.

00:19:10.207 --> 00:19:11.917
Prosecutor,
your opening statement?

00:19:12.001 --> 00:19:13.418
Yeah, honey,
I'll be home for dinner.

00:19:13.502 --> 00:19:15.086
The prosecution rests,
Your Honor.

00:19:15.171 --> 00:19:16.254
Very well.

00:19:16.339 --> 00:19:19.966
We will reconvene when the jury reaches a verdict.

00:19:25.848 --> 00:19:28.850
Son, you in
a whole mess of trouble.

00:19:40.112 --> 00:19:41.112
What?

00:19:41.197 --> 00:19:43.448
Has the jury reached
a verdict?

00:19:43.532 --> 00:19:45.116
No, we have not,

00:19:45.284 --> 00:19:48.536
for we have evolved to a
higher state of consciousness.

00:19:48.829 --> 00:19:53.249
In the grand scheme, all
physical beings are but yokels.

00:19:53.334 --> 00:19:56.670
Now, settle your petty
squabbles and get the hell out.

00:19:59.674 --> 00:20:01.549
That'll be $10,000.

00:20:12.561 --> 00:20:15.188
Well, digital photographs
don't lie.

00:20:15.272 --> 00:20:19.275
I admit that what you witnessed may
have been some form of evolution.

00:20:19.360 --> 00:20:21.820
I'm glad you agree,
Dr. Banjo.

00:20:21.904 --> 00:20:25.699
Evolution set in motion by a
wise and all-knowing creator.

00:20:25.783 --> 00:20:26.783
You.

00:20:26.951 --> 00:20:30.286
Well, I don't know
about all-knowing.

00:20:30.371 --> 00:20:33.039
And I admit it's possible,
however unlikely,

00:20:33.124 --> 00:20:36.042
that some wise
and all-knowing alien monster

00:20:36.127 --> 00:20:38.712
set evolution in motion
here on Earth.

00:20:38.796 --> 00:20:41.464
Oh, oh, and the creator
could also be a robot.

00:20:41.549 --> 00:20:45.301
Then who built
this so-called creator robot?

00:20:45.386 --> 00:20:47.804
Some magical bearded robot
in the sky?

00:20:49.598 --> 00:20:52.350
I guess that would be stupid. Never mind.

00:20:52.435 --> 00:20:53.601
Then it's settled.

00:20:53.686 --> 00:20:57.897
Finally, a world in which
I'm happy to raise my son.

00:20:58.107 --> 00:21:00.233
Good, 'cause I'm
sick of him.

00:21:03.279 --> 00:21:05.905
I'm serious.
He's a terrible person.